  "mechanistic_conclusion": "Disentangled Ego-Motion and Memory Dynamics. Offline calibration with corrected t -> t+1 alignment shows the learned sensor displacement head has minimal predictive gain (MAE 0.0274m, R^2 = 0.0143 on magnitude regression) over the zero baseline (0.0287m). In contrast, the action-conditioned predictor improves translation prediction (MAE 0.0142m, R^2 = 0.2549 on magnitude regression). Under hold/freeze dead-reckoning, Action Hold (0.5490m) is equivalent to Oracle Hold (0.5368m) only within the specified 0.05m margin (TOST p = 6.85e-07) and tested simulation conditions, significantly outperforming zero hold (0.6499m, p = 8.09e-09) and shuffled action (0.5768m, p = 1.49e-04). Fixed-blending vs hold tracking differences (paired diff 0.0549m, 95% CI: [-0.0416, 0.1528]m, Wilcoxon p = 0.1719) are not statistically significant. The controller buffer is handwritten integration logic, not learned recurrent state."
